s across the district.\n\nEvery major race rating, from the Cook Political Report to Sabato's Crystal Ball, places the district in the solid or safe Republican column. The two publicly available polls, conducted in late September, showed Langworthy ahead by 17 and 21 points among likely voters, and prediction markets give Gies roughly a two percent chance. The national environment leans Democratic this year, which may narrow the margin somewhat, but the structural advantages in this seat remain firmly with Langworthy.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0384, "margin": -14.25}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0469, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0245, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0293, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0214, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.028, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0212, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0226, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0153, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0374, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0205, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0162, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0247, "margin": -14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0197, "margin": -14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.02, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0177, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.017, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.0208, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.0114, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.0249, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.0331, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-13", "p_dem": 0.0233, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-14", "p_dem": 0.0217, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-15", "p_dem": 0.0186, "margin": -15.5}, {"date": "2026-10-16", "p_dem": 0.0413, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-